<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Glass control capsule (2026-10-23 片 072): the floating tab bar's face, taken off bg_glass_bar. Since
  片 075 it is also the face of the two pinned top bars (home, library) - see the reason below.

  Why a sixth face instead of raising chrome: the pill's labels sit on top of someone else's text -
  a card title scrolling underneath reads through a 74% fill, and the pair of layers blurs into one
  illegible band. That is the failure mode the user reported, so this face stops trading against the
  transparency claim and takes the reader's alpha (.93). Chrome keeps .74 for the top bars that scroll
  with their own page (chat, navigation), where the ratified decision still stands; the moment a bar
  is pinned over a moving column it becomes the same case as the tab bar, which is why the home and
  library bars joined it on 片 075.

  Flat, not tinted: bg_glass_bar's 145° diagonal darkens its lower end to alpha × falloff (.74 × .54),
  which is the darker half of exactly the band where the overlap was worst. A 52-62dp capsule cannot
  carry that gradient and stay legible; the sheen and the 1px edge stay, so the light source is still
  the same one every other face here paints.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item>
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <gradient
                android:angle="270"
                android:endColor="@android:color/transparent"
                android:startColor="@color/glass_sheen" />
            <corners android:radius="@dimen/radius_full" />
        </shape>
    </item>
    <item>
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <solid android:color="@color/glass_control" />
            <stroke android:width="@dimen/hairline" android:color="@color/glass_edge" />
            <corners android:radius="@dimen/radius_full" />
        </shape>
    </item>
</layer-list>
